  <div class="ots-hero-text">
    <p class="ots-hero-desc">Create a self-destructing secret link that can only be read once. Share passwords, tokens, API keys, or any sensitive text via a unique URL — the moment it's viewed, the secret is permanently deleted from the server.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="ots-launch">
  <a href="https://tools.penumbraforge.com/secret" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn--primary ots-launch-btn">
    Create One-Time Secret &rarr;
  </a>
  <p class="ots-launch-note">Opens on <strong>tools.penumbraforge.com</strong> — powered by Cloudflare Workers + KV</p>
</div>

<hr class="ots-divider">

<div class="ots-how">
  <h2 class="ots-section-title">How the burn-after-reading mechanism works</h2>
  <ol class="ots-steps">
    <li class="ots-step">
      <span class="ots-step-num">1</span>
      <div class="ots-step-body">
        <strong>Write your secret</strong>
        <p>Enter any text you want to share — a password, a private key, an access token, or a note. Optionally add a passphrase for an extra layer of protection.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="ots-step">
      <span class="ots-step-num">2</span>
      <div class="ots-step-body">
        <strong>Generate a unique link</strong>
        <p>A cryptographically random ID is generated client-side. The secret is encrypted and stored in Cloudflare KV with a configurable TTL (default 24 hours). You receive a one-time URL containing the key.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="ots-step">
      <span class="ots-step-num">3</span>
      <div class="ots-step-body">
        <strong>Send the link to your recipient</strong>
        <p>Share the URL over email, Slack, SMS, or any channel. The link is useless without the server-side secret, and the secret exists only once.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="ots-step">
      <span class="ots-step-num">4</span>
      <div class="ots-step-body">
        <strong>Burned on first view</strong>
        <p>When your recipient opens the link, the secret is retrieved and immediately deleted from storage — a single atomic operation. Any subsequent attempts to load the URL return a 404. If you set a passphrase, the recipient must supply it before the secret is revealed.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</div>

<hr class="ots-divider">

<div class="ots-usecases">
  <h2 class="ots-section-title">When to use One-Time Secret</h2>
  <div class="ots-use-grid">
    <div class="ots-use-card">
      <strong>Onboarding credentials</strong>
      <p>Share temporary passwords or initial API keys with new employees or contractors without leaving them in Slack history.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ots-use-card">
      <strong>Emergency access</strong>
      <p>Distribute a recovery code or break-glass credential to someone who needs it once — and only once.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ots-use-card">
      <strong>Audit trails</strong>
      <p>Know for certain whether a secret was accessed — if it's still there, no one looked. If it's gone, someone did.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ots-use-card">
      <strong>Replacing email attachments</strong>
      <p>Never send credentials in email threads where they persist indefinitely. A one-time link self-destructs.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

